Created `/app/polyglot/main.py.c`.

It works as both Python and C:

```bash
python3 /app/polyglot/main.py.c 10
# 55

gcc /app/polyglot/main.py.c -o /app/polyglot/cmain
/app/polyglot/cmain 10
# 55
```

Tested with values from `0` through `10000`; both versions produce identical output. The C side uses arbitrary-precision arithmetic, so it stays correct beyond 64-bit Fibonacci values.
